# Force LF line endings for the tab-delimited/XML smoke-test fixtures that
# crux's own parsers read or that get compared byte/line-exact against
# crux's output, regardless of a developer's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# crux's tab-delimited reader (StringUtils::FromString, used via
# MatchFileReader) does not tolerate a trailing \r on the last column of a
# line. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, these text fixtures
# get silently converted from the committed LF to CRLF, so the last numeric
# column of every row throws "Could not convert string '...'" and fails
# nearly every smoke-test scenario that parses or compares them
# (assign-confidence, make-pin, percolator, psm-convert, tide-index, ...).
#
# Deliberately scoped to an allow-list of known-text extensions rather than
# a blanket "* eol=lf" with binary exceptions: once "eol" is set on a path
# it forces line-ending normalization for that path even if a later pattern
# also sets "-text" on it, so a catch-all rule risks corrupting genuinely
# binary fixtures (.mzML, .hk, .ms1, spectrumrecords, the compiled
# standard2_crux_index/* protobuf index, ...) that this repo also carries.
*.txt text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.pin text eol=lf
*.sqt text eol=lf
*.mzid text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.ms2 text eol=lf
